tent": [{"type": "text", "content": "D.1 Table Recognition . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 36 D.2 Formula Recognition . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 36 D.3 Image-Aware Parsing . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 36"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.495, 0.92, 0.505, 0.932], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "2"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 2, "blocks": [{"type": "header", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.138, 0.061, 0.721, 0.076], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "MinerU2.5-Pro: Pushing the Limits of Data-Centric Document Parsing at Scale"}]}, {"type": "image", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.139, 0.076, 0.861, 0.473], "content": [{"type": "image_body", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.139, 0.076, 0.861, 0.473], "content": "End-to-End Performance\n100\nMinerU2.5-Pro\n95.69 95.15 94.87\n95.69\n95\n93.68 93.62 93.27 93.20 92.98 92.85\nMinerU2.5\n90.64 90.50 90.17 89.87 89.78 89.34 88.44 88.43\n90\nGLM-OCR\n86.52\n85\nPaddleOCR-VL-1.5\nYoutu-Parsing\n80\nOvis2.6-30B-A3B\n75\nFireRed-OCR\n70\nOmniDocBench-v1.6 [Full Overall]\nLogics-Parsing-v2\n100\n100\n96.19 96.12 95.72 94.87 94.56 94.16 94.14 93.23 93.04 92.96\n96.12        94.08\nGemini-3 Pro\n94.08\n95\n92.01 92.01 91.99 91.65 90.39 89.95 89.89 89.81 88.67\n95\nOpenDoc-0.1B\n90\n90\n85\ndots.ocr\n80\n85\nDeepSeek-OCR 2\nOmniDocBench-v1.6 [Base Overall]        OmniDocBench-v1.6 [Hard Overall]\nHunyuanOCR\nSingle-task Performance\n1-Edit        CDM        TEDS        1-Edit\nQwen3-VL-235B\n100\n100\n100\n100\n95\nDolphin-v2\n98\n98\n97.29 96.99 96.69\n97.29\n95\n93.42 92.83 92.02 91.67 91.01\n93.42\n96.49 96.37 96.28 96.24 95.93\n96.37\n88.39 87.97 87.04 87.01 86.91\n90\n87.97\n95.83 95.59\n96\n96\nOCRVerse\n90\n85\n94\n94\n80\nMonkeyOCR-pro-3B\n85\n92\n92\n75\n80\n90\n90\n70\nGPT-5.2\nText Block [Full]        Formula [Full]        Table [Full]        Reading Order [Full]"}, {"type": "image_caption", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.137, 0.515, 0.864, 0.605], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Figure 1: Performance comparison on OmniDocBench v1.6, which comprises Base (standard samples), Hard (challenging samples), and Full (overall) splits. Built upon MinerU2.5 [25] with its 1.2B-parameter architecture entirely unchanged, MinerU2.5-Pro improves the overall score from 92.98 to 95.69 purely through data engineering and training strategy design, outperforming both specialized document parsing models (e.g. GLM-OCR [11], PaddleOCR-VL-1.5 [8], Youtu-Parsing[45]) and general-purpose VLMs (e.g. Gemini 3 Pro, Qwen3-VL-235B [43]). Detailed results are presented in Table 2."}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.138, 0.629, 0.311, 0.645], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "1 Introduction"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.138, 0.662, 0.862, 0.752], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Document parsing converts unstructured documents such as PDFs into structured, machine-readable formats (e.g. Markdown), serving as critical infrastructure for LLM training data pipelines [49, 29, 35] and retrieval-augmented generation systems [15, 37, 48]. As end-to-end approaches based on visionlanguage models (VLMs) progressively replace traditional pipeline systems [2, 39, 25], research has focused predominantly on architectural innovation and inference efficiency, leading to rapid score convergence among top models on standard benchmarks."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.137, 0.76, 0.863, 0.865], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Yet this convergence raises a deeper question: what constitutes the remaining performance bottleneck? Our cross-analysis of parsing results from multiple state-of-the-art models—spanning diverse architectures and parameter scales—on large-scale real-world PDFs reveals a striking pattern: these models exhibit highly similar failure modes on the same hard samples, with certain parsing errors common to all tested systems. Since these systematic failures transcend any particular architecture, they point to a common root cause: the current performance bottleneck in document parsing stems primarily from shared deficiencies in training data, not from model architecture itself."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.137, 0.873, 0.864, 0.888], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This data bottleneck manifests in two interrelated dimensions. First, insufficient coverage: for instance,"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.495, 0.92, 0.505, 0.932], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "3"}]}]}], "is_full_document": false, "schema": "docvortex.middle", "schema_version": "2.0"}